# Copy this file to Finance/.env and fill in your key.
# Finance/.env is git-ignored; this .example file is safe to commit.

# Powers the AI features in Finance, all optional — without a key each
# button just returns a "not configured" message and everything else works:
#   * "Extract details with AI" on the Add / Update record forms
#   * "Ask AI whether to buy" on each Shopping List item
#   * "Suggest from item" (category) on the Add form  — tries your own
#     history first (free), only calls the AI as a fallback
#   * "Generate AI review" on the Summary page (cached per month)
#   * "Next month's income" estimate on the Summary page (has a free
#     statistical baseline; the key only adds an AI-refined range)
#   * "Can I afford…?" on the Dashboard
# (Unusual-transaction flagging on the Dashboard is pure statistics — no key needed.)
# Get one at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here

# Optional: override the OpenAI model used for all of the above.
# OPENAI_RECEIPT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Signs the profile-switcher session cookie (which profile is "you" on this
# browser). Works without setting this — falls back to a fixed dev value —
# but set a real random string before this leaves your machine, since anyone
# who knows the fallback could forge another profile's session cookie.
# Generate one with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
# FLASK_SECRET_KEY=
